          "concern": "The request URL scope was mistaken for permissions granted by the user.",
          "response": "The author explains that the authorization URL carries all requested scopes. The final fake names requestedScope, expectedScope and grantedScope separately and simulates user choices with checkboxes.",
          "applied": "The complete landed helper diff checks requested URL scope, selects granted checkboxes, stores their submitted values with tokens and returns granted scope. IMAP token validation enforces test_mail; tests cover none, mail-only, non-mail and all scopes.",
          "outcome": "The request badge remains Not Done; the author reply is Done and aleca later explicitly accepts with a tests-pass report. No inference that acceptance changes the badge. This supports scoped role naming and behavior, not a new user instruction."
        },
        {
          "concern": "Removing the granular consent feature switch prevents exercising the flow on all channels.",
          "response": "The author requests retaining the endpoint- and preference-gated switch until the feature is enabled by default; the reviewer acknowledges its mistaken removal.",
          "applied": "The landing adds enable_granular_consent=true only for the Google authorization endpoint and enabled mailnews.oauth.granular preference.",
          "outcome": "Both inline markers are Done. This is a historical channel-testing requirement; later provider defaults are not inferred."
        },
        {
          "concern": "Persisting requested scopes can claim permissions the token does not have; beta reports may miss provider rollout conditions.",
          "response": "The bug specifies account, address-book, calendar and restart cases. Comment4 reports manual WIP checks; comment21 says Google was not showing granular consent to beta users and the author changed user agent while testing the five related patches.",
          "applied": "The source tests check granted scope in returned configuration, saved login realm and persisted incoming/outgoing server preferences after clearing cached OAuth objects. Browser task names and registration remain linked as the existing scoped lesson records.",
          "outcome": "Keep these as historical reports. ESR128 uplift was later backed out; comment27 explicitly restores fixed for central while ESR repair remains unresolved. Do not infer ESR success from bug fixed state. Linked regression bugs are covered separately or remain unread here."
        },
